Third-party material
====================

Bundled in this repository
--------------------------

davey (crates/vendor/davey/)
  Rust implementation of Discord's DAVE protocol, vendored with patches for openmls 0.9 and
  WebAssembly (see crates/vendor/davey/VENDORED.md).
  MIT License, see crates/vendor/davey/LICENSE.

openmls_memory_storage (crates/vendor/openmls_memory_storage/)
  The OpenMLS project's in-memory key store, vendored with a patch that notes the keys it changes
  (see crates/vendor/openmls_memory_storage/VENDORED.md).
  MIT License, see crates/vendor/openmls_memory_storage/LICENSE.

Photo backgrounds (assets/backgrounds/)
  Sixteen pictures for background replacement, cropped and scaled by scripts/process-backgrounds.py.
  Each is dedicated to the public domain (CC0 1.0) or marked public domain by its author
  (Public Domain Mark 1.0); no attribution is required. Title, author, source URL, licence and
  retrieval date of every picture: assets/backgrounds/SOURCES.md.
  CC0 1.0: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
  Authors: Wilfredor, Lo, Mertbiol, Foto Miki (Foto Miki Digital), National Chiao Tung University,
  FelixM, Ted Moravec.

Interface fonts (crates/teamcraft-ui/fonts/, apps/android/app/src/main/res/font/, also in the iOS app)
  Inter, Google Sans Flex, IBM Plex Sans, Source Sans 3, Atkinson Hyperlegible Next, Lexend,
  OpenDyslexic, Noto Sans and JetBrains Mono, for the font setting (#1494). Each under the SIL Open
  Font License 1.1; IBM Plex ("Plex"), Source Sans 3 ("Source") and OpenDyslexic have Reserved Font
  Names and are shipped unmodified, the others are subset by scripts/build-fonts.py. Versions,
  sources and copyright holders: crates/teamcraft-ui/fonts/NOTICE.md; licence texts:
  crates/teamcraft-ui/fonts/licenses/.

Shipped with the apps, not stored in git
----------------------------------------

MediaPipe selfie segmentation model (background effects)
  Copyright Google LLC. Apache License 2.0, https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
  Fetched at packaging time with a pinned checksum, see crates/teamcraft-media/models/NOTICE.md.

Downloaded by the apps at runtime
---------------------------------

OpenH264 Video Codec provided by Cisco Systems, Inc.
  The apps download Cisco's prebuilt binary directly from Cisco (ciscobinary.openh264.org) on
  first use, so Cisco's H.264 patent license applies. TeamCraft does not distribute it.

Rust dependencies
-----------------

Dependencies from crates.io keep their own licenses; `cargo deny check licenses` enforces the
allow list in deny.toml. Desktop and mobile builds list them on their about/licenses screen.

Design references
-----------------

The device linking handshake (crates/teamcraft-crypto/src/rendezvous.rs) is modelled on the
connection rendezvous protocol described in Threema's cryptography whitepaper; no Threema code is
included. Calls use Discord's DAVE protocol design (via davey above).
